SOAPBOX: Enjoyable contest despite the elevated K-index and impact on
SOAPBOX: CONDX. Interesting propagation on 10m including LP from CN in the
SOAPBOX: mornings, but nothing heard of South America at all. Heard but
SOAPBOX: couldn't work 4Z, 5W, A3 and S5 on 10m. Went to 40m
SOAPBOX: and 80m on Saturday night (VK2 time) to hand out some numbers,
SOAPBOX: with high QRN due to electrical storm activity. Station consisted of
SOAPBOX: TS-2000 at 100W output, 5-band spiderbeam at 10m height for 10m,
SOAPBOX: 2x 3-el reversible yagis at about 15m for 40m, and inverted V at
SOAPBOX: 15m for 80m. Thanks to all those who answered my calls, my
SOAPBOX: apologies to anyone I missed, and thanks to the managers for
SOAPBOX: running the contest.
